   :ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: todo
   :ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
   :END:
   Switched from per-batch BatchConfirmation to per-tx
   Confirmation(Hash<Tx>) for the roundtrip.  Server now hashes each
   tx in the committed batch, looks up its originating client, and
   sends one Confirmation per tx.  Stressor stores per-tx send_ts.
   Verified: Zeus 68.9 ms latency, Leto 79.5 ms (was NaN).  Committed
   in 4dfe60e.


* DONE Zeus commit-stall in orchestrator local smoke :Zeus:Correctness:
   CLOSED: [2026-05-18 Sun]
   :PROPERTIES:
   :ARCHIVE_TIME: 2026-05-20 Wed 09:15
   :ARCHIVE_FILE: ~/Github/leto-rs/todo.org
   :ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Known regressions (2026-05-18)
   :ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: todo
   :ARCHIVE_TODO: DONE
   :END:
   Root cause: eleader proposed empty data blocks on every batcher
   tick (libmempool seals on batch_timeout even with no txs).  Every
   committed payload was empty → counter stayed 0.  Sig-chain commit
   machinery was working all along (~400 FIRING events confirmed via
   instrumentation).  Fix: on_eleader_propose drops empty batches
   before they reach the chain (consensus/src/server/zeus/phases/data.rs).
   Verified: Zeus orchestrator smoke now produces 9.8k tx/s real
   throughput.  No regression on Leto (still 39k tx/s).
   Committed in 27e0f16.

